<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Uncalibrated camera add-on for the GATR2 robot: the front camera before
any intrinsic or mount calibration exists, so live images and 2D tag
decodes can be inspected in the viewer. Nothing in this file is a
measurement.

The Capture values are selections, not calibration. The intrinsic
calibration must later be done at this same mode: the camera resource
refuses a calibration whose resolution differs from the capture mode.
Change them to a supported mode from the rpicam-hello camera listing on the Pi
before calibrating. Without a Calibration element the frames carry null
intrinsics, the detector decodes tags in 2D with has_pose false, and no
metric tag pose or landmark evidence is ever produced from them; the
viewer labels this state metric unavailable.

robot_geometry is deliberately empty: the camera mount is unmeasured and
the noop association in camera_inspection_only.xml needs no frames. It
keeps the resource ids of gatr2_front_camera.xml so a profile swaps to the
measured fragment without a pipeline change.

Needs a binary built with -DNAVIGATR_WITH_LIBCAMERA=ON; elsewhere the
build fails naming the missing backend. Not yet run on the Pi.
-->
<Robot>

    <Resources>
        <Resource id="robot_geometry" type="robot_frame_map"/>

        <Resource id="front_camera_device" type="libcamera_camera">
            <Device index="0"/>
            <Capture width_px="1280" height_px="960" pixel_format="Y8"
                     frame_rate_hz="30"/>
        </Resource>

        <!-- The size only matters for metric poses, which are unavailable
             without calibration. It is the detector-corner edge inferred
             for tagCircle21h7 from the CAD (docs/field_assets.md) and must
             be measured on a physical goal. -->
        <Resource id="tag_detector" type="apriltag_detector">
            <Family name="tagCircle21h7" detection_size_m="0.01761272"/>
        </Resource>
    </Resources>

    <Sensors>
        <Sensor id="front_camera" type="camera_frame">
            <Source resource_id="front_camera_device" output_id="frame"/>
        </Sensor>
    </Sensors>

</Robot>
